.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd August 23, 2026
.Dt SATL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm satl
.Nd Docker-compatible container engine CLI
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm satl
.Op Fl \-host Ar URL
.Ar command
.Op Ar args ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the command-line client of SatL, a Docker-compatible container engine
for FreeBSD.
It is a thin REST client for
.Xr satld 8 :
every verb maps onto Docker Engine API requests on the daemon socket, and
.Nm
never speaks the cluster's internal protocol.
Any Docker client pointed at the same socket works the same way.
.Pp
The one global option:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl \-host Ar URL
Daemon socket to connect to (docker-style URL).
When the flag is absent the
.Ev DOCKER_HOST
environment variable is read; the default is
.Ql unix:///var/run/satl.sock .
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm version
Show the SatL version information (client and server).
.It Cm run
Create and run a new container from an image.
.It Cm ps
List containers.
.It Cm stop
Stop one or more running containers.
.It Cm kill
Kill one or more running containers.
.It Cm rm
Remove one or more containers.
.It Cm wait
Block until one or more containers stop, then print their exit codes.
.It Cm logs
Fetch the logs of a container.
.It Cm exec
Execute a command in a running container.
.It Cm inspect
Return low-level information on containers.
.It Cm events
Get real-time events from the daemon.
.It Cm info
Display system-wide information about this node's daemon.
.It Cm pull
Download an image from a registry.
.It Cm push
Push an image from this node's store to a registry (client-side, like
satl build).
.It Cm tag
Create a tag TARGET_IMAGE that refers to SOURCE_IMAGE.
.It Cm build
Build a FreeBSD image from a Satlfile into this node's store.
.It Cm images
List images, or manage them (ls, rm, prune, inspect).
.It Cm rmi
Remove one or more images.
Alias of
.Ql satl images rm .
.It Cm container
Manage containers \-\- the verbs that have no top-level spelling.
.It Cm volume
Manage volumes.
.It Cm network
Manage networks.
.It Cm system
Manage SatL itself.
.It Cm swarm , cluster
Manage the swarm.
The
.Cm cluster
spelling is an accepted alias of this verb.
.It Cm ca
View and rotate the cluster root CA (docker's swarm ca, as its own verb:
certificate operations deserve better than a flag pile).
.It Cm node
Manage swarm nodes.
.It Cm compose
Deploy a Compose file on this node (use satl stack for the cluster).
.It Cm service
Manage services.
.It Cm stack
Manage stacks \-\- deploy a Compose file across the cluster (use satl compose
for this node alone). A stack is one compose file's services and networks, on
a shared overlay, placed by the scheduler.
.It Cm secret
Manage secrets.
.It Cm config
Manage configs.
.El
.Pp
Per-verb flags and subcommands are described by
.Ql satl <verb> \-\-help
and, in more depth, by the SatL manual at
.Lk https://docs.satl.cc/ .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/run/satl.sock
The daemon's Docker REST API socket, the default
.Fl \-host
target.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 on success and non-zero when a verb fails.
.Cm run ,
.Cm exec
and
.Cm wait
forward the container's or executed command's exit code instead of
reporting their own.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Run an nginx container in the background and publish port 80:
.Dl satl run \-d \-\-name web \-p 8080:80 nginx:1.27
.Pp
List running containers:
.Dl satl ps
.Pp
Create a replicated cluster service:
.Dl satl service create \-\-name web \-\-replicas 3 \-p 8080:80 nginx:1.27
.Pp
Follow a container's log:
.Dl satl logs \-f web
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr satld.toml 5 ,
.Xr satld 8
.Pp
.Lk https://docs.satl.cc/ "SatL manual"
